# The Moret–Bailly supply chain, hoisted out of `Modularity/KhareWintenberger.lean`

This module is the RELOCATED first half of `Modularity/KhareWintenberger.lean`
(2026-07-27, "Break D"). Nothing here is new mathematics: every declaration was
moved VERBATIM, without reindentation or restatement, from that file's lines
596–23408, in its original order.

## Why the move was necessary

`HardlyRamified/HilbertModularity.lean`'s leaf
`nonempty_potentialHeckeDatum_of_five_le` must PRODUCE a `PotentialHeckeDatum`,
and five of its six obligations are exactly what
`exists_moretBailly_seed_of_five_le` delivers. But the import graph ran
`KhareWintenberger → HardlyRamified/Deformation → HilbertModularity`, so the
whole chain sat strictly DOWNSTREAM of the leaf and could never be consumed —
the layering break recorded in that leaf's docstring as BREAK D. It is repaired
by putting the chain in this module, which is upstream of `HilbertModularity`
and free of everything below it, and having both `HilbertModularity.lean` and
`KhareWintenberger.lean` import it.

## What is here

Lines 596–23408 of the old `KhareWintenberger.lean`, i.e. everything from
`PotentialModularityWitness` down to and including
`exists_moretBailly_seed_of_five_le`:

* the interface structures `PotentialModularityWitness`, `MoretBaillySeed`,
  `HilbertBlumenthalPoint`;
* the Bertini/dimension-drop cut (`section BertiniLeaves`,
  `exists_bertiniHyperplane_of_affine_geometricallyIrreducible`,
  `exists_dimensionDrop_of_affine_geometricallyIrreducible`,
  `exists_affineCurve_of_affine_geometricallyIrreducible`) and the
  supporting algebraic geometry;
* the Moret–Bailly curve leaves (`exists_normalSplitPoint_of_affine_curve`,
  `exists_normalRealPoint_of_affine_curve`, both
  `exists_totallyReal_point_*` wrappers);
* the twisted Hilbert–Blumenthal moduli and dihedral input, up to
  `exists_hilbertBlumenthalPoint_of_five_le`,
  `exists_heckeEigensystem_of_hilbertBlumenthalPoint` and the seed assembly
  `exists_moretBailly_seed_of_five_le`.

`KhareWintenberger.lean` keeps everything from the modularity-lifting cut
(`exists_heckePackage_of_seed`) onwards, plus pillar α's
`exists_hardlyRamified_lift_residual_of_five_le`, and imports this module.

## The two HOISTED clusters at the top of this file

The chain was NOT self-contained: exactly three constant references pointed
DOWNSTREAM, and each is repaired by moving its definition here, in namespace
`GaloisRepresentation` (its original namespace), ahead of the chain:

* `finite_moduleEnd_finTwoFun`, `discreteTopology_moduleEnd_finTwoFun`,
  `isOpen_setOf_framedGaloisRep_eq`, `framedGaloisRepOfMatrix`,
  `apply_framedGaloisRepOfMatrix`, `toMatrix'_framedGaloisRepOfMatrix` —
  moved from `HardlyRamified/Deformation.lean` (lines 5959–6052), used by
  `exists_dihedralOddGaloisRep_of_charThree` below. They depend on nothing in
  `Deformation.lean`; `Deformation.lean` still sees them through
  `HilbertModularity.lean`.
* the residue-degree adapter cluster `norm_padic_le_one_of_ringOfIntegers` …
  `natCard_residue_eq_of_nonempty_ringHom_padic` — moved from
  `HilbertModularity.lean` (lines 11614–11791), where it had itself been
  relocated on 2026-07-27 for the same layering reason, one level too low. It
  is used here by `natCard_residue_eq_of_isTotallySplitAt`, and
  `HilbertModularity.lean` still sees it through this module's import.

Their own section docstrings are preserved verbatim below.

## Imports

This module's import block is `KhareWintenberger.lean`'s, MINUS the two
proof-only imports `HardlyRamified/Deformation` and
`HardlyRamified/Threeadic` — which are precisely the edges that made the old
layering circular. Nothing else was added or removed; the hoisted clusters
elaborate against this list unchanged.
-/
