that file. A fourth, layering break, which no audit had recorded.

They were then moved into `HilbertModularity.lean` itself, and moved once more,
the same day, into THIS module when the whole Moret–Bailly chain was hoisted here
(the Break-D hoist). This is their final home and the reason is that it is the
only one that serves BOTH consumers at once: `natCard_residue_eq_of_isTotallySplitAt`
below, which is Moret–Bailly vocabulary and therefore lives in this module, and
